# Claude Code — ignore most local agent state, but skills/ is project
# content (custom slash-commands checked into the repo).
# `**/` keeps it matching at any depth, and excluding the *contents* rather than the
# directory is what lets the negation work — git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is itself excluded, so a bare `.claude/` would silently defeat `!…/skills/`.
**/.claude/*
!**/.claude/skills/
